{"actor": "opencode-space-bunny", "data": {"documentation_gaps": {"HYPOTHESES.md": ["experiment_result"]}, "duration_s": 5088.7, "landed_paths": 0, "missing_artifacts": 0, "next": "The line's binding obstacle is now named and is a buildable engineering problem, not a research one: a classifier that covers its population with a coverage floor declared before the run, a matched harvest as the default design, and a stratified reading beside the pooled one. If the mission wants a candidate rather than a repaired instrument, this line should stay closed and the next session should open a fresh observation in a domain chosen for a practical problem, not for platform coverage.", "outcome": "worked", "push_requested": false, "summary": "E110 tested whether the view-count principle survives a matched harvest, and answered no. Reading committed bytes first: E107 drew its need arm from topic:web-framework and its random arm from topic:utils, both star-sorted, so its published Cliff's delta=0.826010 (reproduced exactly from its own data) compares the most-starred web frameworks to the most-starred utility libraries. Under a matched harvest on the same platform: within-stratum delta=+0.0746, stratified permutation p=0.183 over 20k iters, 5 of 7 strata negative or zero. A second defect is the binding obstacle: the shared classifier matches unanchored substrings (ai inside email, base inside database) and labels only 196 of 700 rows (28%), 458 matching neither vocabulary - so a 28 percent screen was reported as a 100 percent measurement, and no coverage gate existed on the line. G0 fired twice; AMENDMENT-2 and -3 record the substring bug, the vocabulary-nesting bug, and the one-word probe edit made after seeing it fail. E107's ALL GATES PASS withdrawn (F116, D105); E090/E095/E102/E103/E108 marked untested on a matched harvest, not confirmed; E109 (Pub.dev) marked superseded, never run. The screen is withdrawn, not the idea.", "unlogged_changes": 1}, "host": "instance-20260717-0947", "kind": "session_end", "schema": "origin.session.event/1", "seq": 50, "session": "2026-10-12-001-test-whether-the-view-count-principle-s", "ts": "2026-10-12T01:29:35+00:00"}
